  "notes": [
    "XOR with one input tied high is an inverter, tied low it is a buffer. That makes it a controlled inverter, which is how you build a selectable-polarity output.",
    "XOR is a one-bit not-equal test, so chaining them gives you a parity generator or a bus comparator.",
    "Same pin arrangement as the 74HC00, 74HC08 and 74HC32.",
    "HC inputs need a level near their own rail. Driving a 5 V part from 3.3 V logic wants the HCT version."
